    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high production today, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 73.66. His matchup against Bieber (5.25 xERA) provides a massive SP skill advantage, further bolstered by an ideal dynamic platoon setup. **Drake Baldwin** follows closely at 67.49, utilizing his prime leadoff spot to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Pfaadt. While **Luis Robert Jr.** (64.28) faces a stiffer test against Alvarez, his inherent ability to impact the score through volume and elite speed makes him a cornerstone of today's outfield. Note that **Andy Pages**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Kyle Tucker** carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations; while they are projected to start, we must monitor official team announcements to ensure these efficiency scores hold, particularly for **Kyle Tucker**, whose value is slightly suppressed by a projected 7th-hole placement.\n\nStrategic benching remains critical in our pursuit of 5x5 efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** was the most difficult exclusion (50.99), ultimately falling short because the opponent\u2019s SP, Williams (2.90 xERA), presents a significant hurdle that drags down his raw projection relative to our higher-scoring starters. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.42) faces a tough draw in Cole, his 41 PA historical BvP edge keeps him in the starting nine over high-floor bench options like **Sam Antonacci** or **Miguel Vargas**. We are currently navigating a thin roster with **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL; as such, we are leaning heavily on the speed and versatility of **Nasim Nunez** (57.62) to maximize our stolen base potential against Stock, despite the modest risk presented by an elite opposing catcher. Monitor the weather in the Matz start, as **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** are locked in against a lefty, and while the platoon splits suggest potential, the underlying volatility of the matchup keeps their scores in the mid-50s.",
